  "result": "Excellent! The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nUpdated `send_notification` in `src/notifier/service.py` to add retry and fallback behavior:\n\n**Key features implemented:**\n1. **Retry logic**: Uses `call_with_retry()` (which already exists) to retry email delivery with at most 3 attempts\n2. **Smart retry policy**: Only retries transient failures (`TransientDeliveryError`); permanent failures propagate immediately\n3. **SMS fallback**: If email fails after retries, falls back to SMS if a phone number exists\n4. **Same retry rules for SMS**: SMS delivery also uses `call_with_retry()` for consistency\n5. **Proper error handling**: \n   - If no phone available, re-raises the email error\n   - If SMS fails, lets the SMS exception propagate unchanged (not wrapped)\n6. **Logging**: Follows the package convention with `get_logger(__name__)`, logging the fallback attempt\n7. **Backward compatible**: Function signature and return value unchanged\n\n**All tests pass:**\n- \u2705 2 acceptance tests (email success, email failure \u2192 SMS fallback)\n- \u2705 13 regression tests (API compatibility, error hierarchy, signatures)",
